PortAudio, PulseAudio host API: the streams can move to another sink.

The streams were created with PA_STREAM_DONT_MOVE: a stream on the default
sink stayed on the sink that was the default when it started, and the sound
server refused to move it (a new default sink, Bluetooth headphones, the
choice of the user in the mixer of the desktop). Without the flag the
server moves it like the stream of any other program. Applied by
scripts/build-appimage.sh.

diff --git a/src/hostapi/pulseaudio/pa_linux_pulseaudio_cb.c b/src/hostapi/pulseaudio/pa_linux_pulseaudio_cb.c
index 1103c98..4acc78c 100644
--- a/src/hostapi/pulseaudio/pa_linux_pulseaudio_cb.c
+++ b/src/hostapi/pulseaudio/pa_linux_pulseaudio_cb.c
@@ -776,8 +776,7 @@ PaError PaPulseAudio_StartStreamCb( PaStream * s )
                                  PA_STREAM_AUTO_TIMING_UPDATE |
                                  PA_STREAM_ADJUST_LATENCY |
                                  PA_STREAM_NO_REMIX_CHANNELS |
-                                 PA_STREAM_NO_REMAP_CHANNELS |
-                                 PA_STREAM_DONT_MOVE;
+                                 PA_STREAM_NO_REMAP_CHANNELS;
 
     if( stream->inputStream )
     {
